  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "Minimum-distance assignment changes the corruption distribution, even with unchanged candidate pools. Separate feasibility recovery from assignment optimization; otherwise changed effects on common support cannot be attributed solely to recovered support.",
    "The exact admissibility predicates, distance formula, reuse scopes and joint constraints remain unspecified. Matching-based pruning is sound only when its graph is a relaxation containing every feasible completion.",
    "Initialize search with any validated greedy solution. This guarantees retention of known feasible blocks when search hits its cap; report feasibility certification and distance optimality separately.",
    "Repeated deterministic optimization on identical pools produces identical interventions. Such repetitions cannot estimate corruption Monte Carlo uncertainty; specify what varies across repetitions and how duplicate assignments are handled.",
    "A category-wide wall-time cap makes retained support depend on execution order and machine load. Specify deterministic work allocation, record unattempted blocks separately, and report support bounds that include unresolved blocks.",
    "Add exhaustive small-instance checks for feasibility, pruning and optimality. Difficulty 4 is plausible only if the existing constraints are explicit and reusable; future potential 7 remains speculative until a bounded pilot measures recovery and cost."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Determine how assignment optimization changes the intervention estimand and how to compare construction methods while controlling replacement distance and common support.",
      "query": "Model perturbation diagnostics replacing history items under fixed admissibility constraints: how do deterministic minimum-cost matching and random feasible assignment sampling change the intervention distribution and sensitivity estimand? Methods for separating feasibility recovery from assignment-selection effects."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Find implementation guidance for sound pruning and independent correctness checks before treating failed search as an infeasibility result.",
      "query": "Constraint satisfaction all-different constraints with additional pairwise constraints: sound bipartite maximum matching pruning, branch-and-bound initialized with feasible incumbent, exhaustive small-instance verification, and distinguishing infeasibility certificates from search limits."
    },
